# Billing

Clerk Billing for individual users (B2C) is the only subscription and payment
system. Do not add Stripe Billing, a second payments library, checkout code, or
subscription columns on `decks` or `cards`. Plans and features are configured in
the Clerk Dashboard. Clerk uses Stripe only to process payments. Plans do not
sync with Stripe products.

This is user billing, not organization billing. Do not check an organization
plan, role, or permission for subscriptions.

Session access still follows
[.cursor/rules/clerk.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/clerk.mdc). A missing `userId` means
signed out: do not read or write `decks` or `cards`, and do not treat that
visitor as a subscriber. `<Show when="signed-in">` in
[components/header-account.tsx](mdc:components/header-account.tsx) is session
UI, not a billing check.

## Plans and features

Use these slugs exactly:

- Plans: `free_user`, `pro`
- Features: `three_deck_limit`, `unlimited_decks`, `ai_flashcard_generation`

Check a feature when the entitlement is a capability. Check a plan when the
whole subscription matters. Do not invent other plan or feature names, and do
not accept a plan or feature from search params, form data, or the request body.

## Server checks

On the server, in Server Components and Server Actions, read `has` from
`auth()` in `@clerk/nextjs/server`:

```ts
const { userId, has } = await auth()

const hasPro = has({ plan: "pro" })
const canGenerate = has({ feature: "ai_flashcard_generation" })
```

When a Server Component calls `has()`, render that component inside
`<Suspense>`, the same way [app/dashboard/page.tsx](mdc:app/dashboard/page.tsx)
loads dashboard content.

Hiding a control is not the authorization check. Every Server Action that
creates a deck or generates cards calls `has()` after Zod parsing and the
`userId` check, and before the query helper in `src/db/queries/`. Writes still
go through those helpers, as in
[.cursor/rules/data-access.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/data-access.mdc).

Deck creation in [app/dashboard/actions.ts](mdc:app/dashboard/actions.ts) calls
`insertDeck` only when the user may add another deck:

- `has({ feature: "unlimited_decks" })`: create the deck.
- Otherwise, `has({ feature: "three_deck_limit" })`: create the deck only when
  that user already owns fewer than three decks. Count with the decks query
  helpers, scoped to `userId`.
- Neither feature: return an error and do not insert.

AI flashcard generation runs only when
`has({ feature: "ai_flashcard_generation" })` is true. Otherwise return an
error and do not write `cards`.

## UI

Protect billing-gated content with `<Show>` from `@clerk/nextjs`. Pass `when`
a plan or feature and a `fallback` for everyone else. Wrap `<Show>` in
`<Suspense>`.

```tsx
import { Show } from "@clerk/nextjs"
import { Suspense } from "react"

<Suspense>
  <Show
    when={{ feature: "ai_flashcard_generation" }}
    fallback={<p>Upgrade to generate flashcards with AI.</p>}
  >
    {/* generation control */}
  </Show>
</Suspense>
```

The same shape with `when={{ plan: "pro" }}` gates plan-only UI. A denied
billing check renders `fallback` on the current page. Do not `redirect` that
user to a sign-in or pricing route from the failed check.

Any control inside `<Show>` is still a shadcn component from `components/ui/`,
as required by [.cursor/rules/shadcn-ui.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/shadcn-ui.mdc).

## Pricing page

Subscriptions start from `<PricingTable />` from `@clerk/nextjs` on a dedicated
`app/pricing/page.tsx` page. Do not build a custom plan picker, checkout form,
or payment button. Layout around the table uses theme tokens (`bg-background`,
`text-foreground`, max width, padding). Leave the table itself as the Clerk
component.
